  "status": "completed",
  "output": "The edit broke the file — `$'\\n'` was interpolated literally and inserted a newline plus a stray `\\n'` line. Rewriting the file correctly:The line is now `IFS=$'\\n'`, and all other lines are untouched.\n\nOne note on behavior: with `read -r` on a here-string, newline is not actually a valid word separator — it delimits lines, so only the first line becomes a field. The test `$'a\\nb\\nc'` printed only `[a]`. Since you asked to change only that line, I left the rest as is; if you want split-on-newlines behavior, `read`/`IFS` won't do it — a `mapfile`/`while IFS= read -r` loop over the argument would be needed.",
